WEBVTT

00:00:04.818 --> 00:00:11.770
Print layout starts with the right paper size. Then use the canvas rulers and guides to place and size elements with control.

00:00:14.559 --> 00:00:18.551
Choose Blank report so we can set up the page before adding content.

00:00:22.383 --> 00:00:31.448
Page size and orientation are separate settings. Choose A4, A5 or A6, then set portrait or landscape. The page updates to match.

00:00:32.783 --> 00:00:41.643
For this example choose A5 landscape. The canvas shows the printable page shape, while the page inspector keeps exact size and margins available.

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:51.595
Add a heading and change its text. Select it to reveal its size and position in the inspector and above the selection.

00:00:55.469 --> 00:01:07.014
Open Canvas settings, switch the ruler to millimeters, and choose a 5 millimeter grid. Grid and object snapping help keep edges aligned; hold Alt or Option while dragging to place something freely.

00:01:12.927 --> 00:01:17.633
Drag the heading into position. It follows your cursor and snaps to the page grid.

00:01:21.466 --> 00:01:26.594
Add a rectangle as a simple shape, then drag it independently to another part of the page.

00:01:28.142 --> 00:01:36.392
Resize the rectangle while holding its corner handle. The outline and measurements update as you drag, so you can judge the new size before releasing.

00:01:41.808 --> 00:01:47.286
Preview the page to check how its paper size, orientation, and placed content print.
